<div class="content-block">
    <p>Security has traditionally been bolted onto software after it was built, tested by a separate team once a release was already nearly finished. DevSecOps rejects that model. It embeds security tooling and security thinking directly into the same pipeline that builds, tests, and deploys code, so that risk is caught the moment it is introduced rather than weeks later.</p>

    <p>By the end of this room, you will understand how pre-commit secret detection, static analysis, dependency scanning, dynamic testing, and infrastructure scanning each cover a different layer of risk, and how to design gates that block what genuinely matters without making the pipeline unusable for development teams. A hands-on practical is included where you configure and run a real gate policy.</p>

