// TASK 3: SAST in Pull Request Gates
$task_contents[3] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Reading Code Without Running It</h2>

    <p>Static Application Security Testing examines source code directly, without executing the application. It looks for known risky patterns such as unsanitized input reaching a database query, weak cryptographic functions, or insecure deserialization, in the same way a proofreader can spot a structural flaw in a script without needing to stage the play.</p>

    <p>Modern pipelines run SAST automatically on every pull request. The scan produces a pass or fail check that appears directly on the PR, and high severity findings block the merge until they are resolved. This gives developers feedback within minutes, while the code is still fresh in their mind.</p>

