// TASK 4: Dependency Scanning with SCA
$task_contents[4] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Your Code Is Not the Only Code You Ship</h2>

    <p>Software Composition Analysis scans the libraries and packages a project depends on, comparing each version against databases of known vulnerabilities. Modern applications often contain far more third-party code than code the team actually wrote, so this dependency layer is a major source of real world risk.</p>

    <p>A dependency can be direct, meaning it is listed explicitly in the project's manifest, or transitive, meaning it was pulled in automatically by one of those direct dependencies. A vulnerability in a transitive dependency still affects the running application even though no one on the team ever typed its name.</p>

    <div class="warning-box">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> Important Limitation</h4>
        <p>Vulnerability databases are updated after a flaw is publicly disclosed. A newly discovered zero-day vulnerability will not appear in SCA results until it has been reported and catalogued.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- SVG: Transitive dependency risk
